{"name":"Wind Speed","hex":"#bfd6d9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wind speed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The local speed of the wind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wind_speed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wind speed","blocks":[{"text":"In meteorology, wind speed, or wind flow speed, is a fundamental atmospheric quantity caused by air moving from high to low pressure, usually due to changes in temperature. Wind speed is now commonly measured with an anemometer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Weather_Station_at_Feilding_Waste_Water_Treatment_Plant.JPG/330px-Weather_Station_at_Feilding_Waste_Water_Treatment_Plant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind_speed","wikidata":"Q1464943"},{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind","wikidata":"Q8094"},{"title":"Speed","blocks":[{"text":"In kinematics, the speed of a moving object is the rate at which the distance travelled by the object changes with time. The average speed of an object in an interval of time is the distance travelled by the object divided by the duration of the interval; the instantaneous speed is the limit of the average speed as the duration of the time interval approaches zero. Speed is the magnitude of velocity, which indicates additionally the direction of motion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Motorcyclist_in_Midtown_Manhattan-L1002704.jpg/330px-Motorcyclist_in_Midtown_Manhattan-L1002704.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speed","wikidata":"Q3711325"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/ERA5_global_mean_wind_speed.png/500px-ERA5_global_mean_wind_speed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/ERA5_global_mean_wind_speed.png/1280px-ERA5_global_mean_wind_speed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/ERA5_global_mean_wind_speed.png/500px-ERA5_global_mean_wind_speed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Global distribution of wind speed at 10m above ground averaged over the years 1991–2020 from the ERA5 dataset.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AERA5_global_mean_wind_speed.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/The_Big_Wind_Anemometer.JPG/500px-The_Big_Wind_Anemometer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/The_Big_Wind_Anemometer.JPG/1280px-The_Big_Wind_Anemometer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/The_Big_Wind_Anemometer.JPG/500px-The_Big_Wind_Anemometer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The original anemometer that measured The Big Wind in 1934 at Mount Washington Observatory","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Big_Wind_Anemometer.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Anemometer-Animation.gif/250px-Anemometer-Animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/97/Anemometer-Animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Anemometer-Animation.gif/250px-Anemometer-Animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern day anemometer used to capture wind speed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnemometer-Animation.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/FT742-DM_Acoustic_resonance_wind_sensor.jpg/500px-FT742-DM_Acoustic_resonance_wind_sensor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/FT742-DM_Acoustic_resonance_wind_sensor.jpg/1280px-FT742-DM_Acoustic_resonance_wind_sensor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/FT742-DM_Acoustic_resonance_wind_sensor.jpg/500px-FT742-DM_Acoustic_resonance_wind_sensor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"FT742-DM acoustic resonance wind sensor, one of the instruments now used to measure wind speed at Mount Washington Observatory","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFT742-DM_Acoustic_resonance_wind_sensor.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Average_daily_wind_speed_reagan_national.png/500px-Average_daily_wind_speed_reagan_national.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Average_daily_wind_speed_reagan_national.png/500px-Average_daily_wind_speed_reagan_national.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca